WEBVTT

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:08.570
I've never done anything bad!

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:12.070
Why can you do such a ridiculous thing?

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:14.530
I won't forgive your incivility.

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:17.240
I'll contact my country immediately!

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.370
The lieutenant will do hara-kiri here
if nothing will be found.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:30.750
Oh, what impressive resolve!

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:33.800
Japanese warriors don't go 
back on their word, right?

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:37.170
Go.

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:25.620
Episode 1: Joker Game (Part 1)

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:27.620
<b>Celebrating
Going off to war
Kobashi</b>

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:27.620
Greater Japan National 
Defense Women's Association

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:30.330
<b>Hisanaga Yasutake</b>

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:34.120
The army has landed at Qingdao!

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:37.720
This program is a work of fiction. 
The characters, organizations, locations, laws, names, 
etc. being portrayed are unrelated to actual events.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:37.620
The army has landed at Qingdao!

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:42.470
<b>Greater East Asia
Cultural Society</b>

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:47.930
<b>Greater East Asia
Cultural Society</b>

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:47.930
Lieutenant Sakuma reporting for duty.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:54.160
Are you stupid?

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:11.000
Who bows while wearing a business suit?

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:18.120
So?

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:22.700
You're the spy General Staff Headquarters sent?

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:24.350
No, sir.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:27.800
I don't engage in cowardly behavior like spying.

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:32.020
Ah, so spies are cowards, huh?

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:36.040
<i>Autumn, 1937.</i>

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:40.280
<i>The Imperial Army, following 
Lieutenant Colonel Yuuki's proposal,</i>

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:45.050
<i>established a clandestine spy training agency.</i>

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:45.370
<b>Greater East Asia
Cultural Society</b>

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:52.360
<i>The histories, names, and even ages
of the prospective agents are all</i>

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:54.760
<i>treated as top-secret information.</i>

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:58.150
<i>They study multiple foreign languages,</i>

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:00.920
<i>medicine, pharmacology,</i>

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:03.880
<i>physics, communications...</i>

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:08.100
<i>Professional thieves and safecrackers 
teach them their techniques.</i>

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:11.350
<i>Gigolos even teach them 
the art of seducing women.</i>

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:13.980
<i>They're tested on a wide range of skills.</i>

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:19.180
<i>But, unbelievably,</i>

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:23.890
<i>none of them are graduates of 
the Imperial Japanese Army Academy.</i>

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:27.650
<i>They graduated from imperial 
universities or ordinary colleges.</i>

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:30.730
<i>In other words, they're all 
so-called ordinary citizens.</i>

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:35.540
<i>They easily complete training 
exercises that push them</i>

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:37.890
<i>to their physical and mental limits.</i>

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:39.710
<i>And then,</i>

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:42.930
<i>finally, only eight people remained.</i>

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:46.140
<i>No...</i>

00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:51.690
<i>Eight monsters.</i>

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:08.450
We're going to town. Would you 
like to come, Sakuma-san?

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:12.630
No, I'll pass.

00:05:17.970 --> 00:05:21.370
<i>Unbelievably, there's no curfew 
here at the dormitory.</i>

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:23.680
<i>Everyone is free to do as he pleases at night.</i>

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:27.800
<i>Everything here is completely different from</i>

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:29.880
<i>the army academy I graduated from.</i>

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:34.760
<i>My academy classmates and I swore that we'd</i>

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:37.360
<i>give our lives for our country if necessary.</i>

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:42.400
<i>I'd gladly give my life to save one of theirs.</i>

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:48.790
<i>But the students here...</i>

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:53.820
<i>Miyoshi.</i>

00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:56.010
<i>Kaminaga.</i>

00:05:56.840 --> 00:05:57.750
<i>Odagiri.</i>

00:05:58.790 --> 00:05:59.550
<i>Amari.</i>

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:01.460
<i>Hatano.</i>

00:06:02.780 --> 00:06:03.670
<i>Jitsui.</i>

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:05.550
<i>Fukumoto.</i>

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:07.560
<i>Tazaki.</i>

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:11.440
<i>They all use false names.</i>

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:15.360
<i>They call each other by fake names, 
respond to fake life stories...</i>

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:18.780
<i>They undergo such harsh training together,</i>

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:21.840
<i>but they don't even know 
each other's real names.</i>

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:27.140
<i>How can they live like that?</i>

00:06:57.820 --> 00:06:59.690
I call. Two pair.

00:07:00.740 --> 00:07:01.710
One pair.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:03.540
One pair here, too.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:06.070
<b>Cafeteria</b>

00:07:04.350 --> 00:07:05.550
You got me.

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:09.610
I'm out.

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:13.520
Oh, you're back?

00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:15.910
What're you doing?

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:18.870
Care to join us, Sakuma-san?

00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:20.970
Poker, huh?

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:24.410
Sure, I'll play a little.

00:07:30.190 --> 00:07:30.970
I'll bet.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:33.930
I call.

00:07:34.650 --> 00:07:35.560
I fold.

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:36.900
Fold.

00:07:38.010 --> 00:07:38.890
I call.

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:52.570
I'll raise you.

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:07.840
I'll raise.

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:08.630
I fold.

00:08:10.470 --> 00:08:11.390
I call.

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:13.930
Full house!

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:17.640
Four of a kind.

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:22.140
I'm just getting started.

00:08:46.010 --> 00:08:49.340
Oh, well. These things happen sometimes.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:51.760
We'll have to do this again.

00:08:56.780 --> 00:09:00.010
Sakuma-san, you didn't lose the poker game.

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:03.630
What do you mean?

00:09:03.630 --> 00:09:06.730
I was peeking at your cards

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:08.480
and signaling the others.

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:09.940
What?!

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:15.700
What's so fun about cheating to win?

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:17.630
We...

00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:21.090
weren't playing poker at all.

00:09:21.090 --> 00:09:24.090
What? Then what were you doing?

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:29.680
We call it the Joker Game.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:33.770
Joker Game?

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:36.500
Basically...

00:09:38.190 --> 00:09:40.840
There's a card game going on at the table,

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:42.990
but it's only a charade.

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:46.190
The goal is to get people 
in the room on your side,

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:49.650
have them peek at the opponents'
hands, and signal you.

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:54.530
However, there's no telling 
who's on whose side.

00:09:55.450 --> 00:09:57.680
The signs may be fake,

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:00.690
or you might read an opponent's 
signs and change your hand.

00:10:02.020 --> 00:10:03.910
Hey, give me a cigarette.

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:05.910
Here.

00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:09.420
In the right conditions, 
you can convince the enemy spy

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:11.710
to betray his side and join yours.

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:15.560
What's so enjoyable about 
deceiving one another like that?

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:17.660
What's the point?!

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:19.210
Who knows?

00:10:19.210 --> 00:10:22.300
It's more or less the same thing 
as international politics.

00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:24.990
International politics?

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:26.170
What's going on?

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:29.400
Just our usual game.

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:32.630
Sakuma-san doesn't like it, that's all.

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:36.000
I'm not complaining about 
who won and who lost.

00:10:36.380 --> 00:10:39.240
My point is that the way 
you do things is cowardly.

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:44.270
You think all competition 
should be fair and square, huh?

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:48.540
If they hadn't let you in on the secret,

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:52.320
would you be saying the things you are now?

00:10:53.180 --> 00:10:56.570
That's the current state of Japan.

00:10:57.660 --> 00:10:59.300
What do you mean by that?

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:03.800
Say this is Washington.

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:08.610
Imagine that table is the stage for 
an international political meeting.

00:11:09.400 --> 00:11:12.880
If your information is leaked, 
you've got no hope of winning.

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:17.610
The same thing happened to 
Japan during last year's

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:19.490
disarmament summit in Washington.

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:30.910
The American 
Black Chamber

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:30.910
<b>Former lead US Cryptologist 
H.O. Yardley's Shocking Documents</b>

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:30.910
<b>American Govt.
Cracks Everything</b>

00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:24.580
From the very beginning, the players 
at that table, the other countries,

00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:29.090
knew exactly how much Japan would be

00:11:29.090 --> 00:11:30.910
willing to compromise.

00:11:32.070 --> 00:11:34.770
Japan was preoccupied with 
the rules for the façade.

00:11:35.270 --> 00:11:39.270
We never even noticed the true 
nature of the game being played.

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:44.850
Remember, this is a spy training facility.

00:11:45.510 --> 00:11:49.900
When these men leave here, 
they'll be scattered all over the world,

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:53.400
where they'll have to make themselves invisible.

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:57.900
Ten years, twenty years, maybe even longer.

00:11:58.450 --> 00:12:00.940
Their job will be to move to a foreign land,

00:12:00.940 --> 00:12:04.740
assimilate, and make themselves invisible

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:06.890
in order to gather intelligence on

00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:09.830
that nation and report back to Japan.

00:12:10.270 --> 00:12:14.090
Can you even imagine what 
their lives will be like?

00:12:15.980 --> 00:12:18.090
The only thing that awaits you all

00:12:19.530 --> 00:12:21.340
is black, empty solitude.

00:12:23.750 --> 00:12:26.080
If you were a spy,

00:12:26.770 --> 00:12:29.890
and the enemy discovered your 
secret, what would you do?

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:33.170
I'd have no choice but to kill the enemy,

00:12:33.170 --> 00:12:35.500
or if that weren't possible, kill myself.

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:40.240
Kill or commit suicide...

00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:43.380
The worst possible decisions a spy can make.

00:12:44.440 --> 00:12:47.160
I don't understand what you're trying to say.

00:12:47.480 --> 00:12:49.340
When someone dies during peacetime,

00:12:49.930 --> 00:12:52.510
their country's police will 
inevitably get involved.

00:12:53.360 --> 00:12:56.590
It should be obvious that, to a spy,

00:12:57.020 --> 00:13:00.240
both murder and suicide are pointless,

00:13:00.240 --> 00:13:02.300
idiotic courses of action.

00:13:02.830 --> 00:13:06.090
That's the way cowards who fear death think.

00:13:07.060 --> 00:13:11.060
I just can't see spies as 
anything but gutless cowards!

00:13:12.860 --> 00:13:14.700
Then let me ask you this.

00:13:14.700 --> 00:13:18.270
If you commit suicide, what happens next?

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:19.440
If I die...

00:13:20.680 --> 00:13:22.990
I'll proudly meet my comrades on the other side.

00:13:23.290 --> 00:13:26.210
Ah. Then you'd die so that

00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:29.430
you could brag about it to your 
compatriots in the afterlife.

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:32.750
But what if you don't see them there?

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:34.910
There's no way that would happen!

00:13:35.390 --> 00:13:36.560
I see.

00:13:37.640 --> 00:13:39.630
Miyoshi. What's your opinion?

00:13:40.190 --> 00:13:43.750
Tautology. "With enough faith,
you can worship a sardine's head."

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:45.950
It's a deeply entrenched belief,

00:13:46.660 --> 00:13:48.860
but no different from a new religion.

00:13:48.860 --> 00:13:50.800
Their ideas are short-lived once they

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:53.080
leave the confines of an isolated group.

00:13:53.920 --> 00:13:55.060
Kaminaga?

00:13:55.440 --> 00:13:57.220
I agree with Miyoshi.

00:13:57.870 --> 00:14:00.670
For example, if Japan lost the war,

00:14:00.670 --> 00:14:03.550
the people would promptly 
learn to take all their faith

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:07.530
and put it in the antithesis 
of their original beliefs.

00:14:09.330 --> 00:14:11.810
<i>If Japan lost the war?!</i>

00:14:12.750 --> 00:14:16.620
Money, honor, patriotism...

00:14:17.310 --> 00:14:20.150
Even death is fiction.

00:14:21.350 --> 00:14:24.730
The only thing that lies in your 
futures is that empty solitude.

00:14:25.980 --> 00:14:29.360
And the only thing you'll have 
to support you there

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:34.280
is your ability to constantly 
adapt to any situation,

00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:38.270
and instantly decide the best course of action.

00:14:43.640 --> 00:14:47.410
<i>So they're not even becoming spies out of</i>

00:14:47.780 --> 00:14:50.290
<i>a sense of honor or patriotism.</i>

00:14:51.610 --> 00:14:55.060
<i>It's just an obscene amount of 
self-confidence telling them,</i>

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:58.120
<i>"I must be able to do this."</i>

00:15:04.150 --> 00:15:05.920
<i>The only ones who could live like that</i>

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:08.700
<i>are monsters.</i>

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:31.290
Give us the order to go in and get proof.

00:15:31.720 --> 00:15:34.030
There's no question this guy's a spy.

00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:38.710
Bring back irrefutable evidence.

00:15:39.510 --> 00:15:40.750
Understand?

00:15:41.470 --> 00:15:42.700
John Gordon.

00:15:43.190 --> 00:15:46.950
He came to Japan three years ago 
at a major trading company's invitation.

00:15:47.410 --> 00:15:49.680
He runs a business here that

00:15:49.680 --> 00:15:52.090
calibrates imported precision machinery.

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:55.600
Currently, he's renting 
a Japanese house in Kanda,

00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:57.590
eats rice out of a bowl with chopsticks,

00:15:57.590 --> 00:16:01.370
prays before the emperor's portrait 
morning and night, and lives as a Japanophile.

00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:05.760
Gordon is suspected to be a spy.

00:16:06.770 --> 00:16:09.120
Another man, arrested in another case,

00:16:09.120 --> 00:16:11.360
named him.

00:16:12.850 --> 00:16:16.760
Colonel Mutou expects this school to

00:16:16.760 --> 00:16:19.700
bring back concrete proof of the target's guilt.

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:24.730
Proof? Why would you bother looking for proof?

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:27.390
Huh? What did you say?

00:16:28.230 --> 00:16:30.510
Even if you don't go look for evidence,

00:16:30.510 --> 00:16:34.110
he'll disappear on his own if you leave him alone.

00:16:35.130 --> 00:16:38.500
Gordon is suspected of the serious crime

00:16:38.500 --> 00:16:43.170
of taking covert pictures of the Imperial 
Japanese Army's cryptographic ciphers.

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:47.910
Once a spy is suspected, he's finished.

00:16:48.850 --> 00:16:52.960
It's as pointless as taking a crippled 
enemy combatant prisoner.

00:16:55.880 --> 00:16:59.450
General Staff HQ is growing 
more vocal in their demands

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:02.090
for results from this school.

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:07.400
In other words, this is an 
official mission for D-Agency.

00:17:07.700 --> 00:17:09.250
A meaningless mission.

00:17:10.290 --> 00:17:12.910
Regardless, orders are orders.

00:17:17.530 --> 00:17:21.250
Fine. All we need is some evidence, right?

00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:27.600
How should we go about it?

00:17:28.390 --> 00:17:30.690
You'll masquerade as a military police unit.

00:17:31.240 --> 00:17:34.530
Miyoshi, you'll take command at the scene.

00:17:35.510 --> 00:17:38.950
As soon as you find evidence, 
get out of there immediately.

00:17:39.710 --> 00:17:42.330
You'll have about forty minutes before

00:17:42.690 --> 00:17:44.690
the real MPs start kicking up a fuss.

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:46.580
Can you do it?

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:49.380
Thirty minutes would be enough.

00:17:49.800 --> 00:17:52.040
Well, Sakuma-san,

00:17:52.040 --> 00:17:54.840
can I ask you to play the role of MP captain?

00:17:55.230 --> 00:17:56.090
Me?

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:59.050
I'll act as your interpreter.

00:17:59.740 --> 00:18:03.270
It would look suspicious if the 
real military police raided

00:18:03.270 --> 00:18:05.840
a foreigner's house without an interpreter.

00:18:06.320 --> 00:18:11.320
I seriously doubt any of them
know a foreign language.

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:15.320
We'll move out at 0800 hours.

00:18:15.750 --> 00:18:17.780
I'll inform the others.

00:18:18.370 --> 00:18:21.740
What're you going to do if we 
don't find anything in the raid?

00:18:23.960 --> 00:18:26.560
Well, it's there, isn't it?

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:34.590
I've never done anything bad!

00:18:35.550 --> 00:18:37.930
Why can you do such a ridiculous thing?

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:40.590
I won't forgive your incivility.

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:43.010
I'll contact my country immediately!

00:18:43.330 --> 00:18:47.160
The lieutenant will do hara-kiri here 
if nothing will be found.

00:18:51.490 --> 00:18:54.000
Oh, what impressive resolve!

00:18:54.300 --> 00:18:57.240
Japanese warriors don't go 
back on their word, right?

00:18:57.240 --> 00:19:00.290
Huh? Hey, what'd you say to him?

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:06.080
I said that if we search his 
house and don't find anything,

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:08.870
you'll cut your own stomach 
open right here, Lieutenant.

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:10.290
What?

00:19:10.590 --> 00:19:13.560
I love Japanese culture!

00:19:14.120 --> 00:19:17.350
I've seen geishas and Fuji Mountain.

00:19:17.350 --> 00:19:19.560
All that's left is a hara-kiri show.

00:19:20.140 --> 00:19:21.700
I can't wait.

00:19:25.830 --> 00:19:26.530
Go.

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:31.900
Hey, take off your shoes! 
Are you even Japanese?!

00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:33.230
Lieutenant!

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:35.650
Order them to take off their shoes!

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:45.200
<i>Why is he so confident?</i>

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:52.420
Stop! Stop it!

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:53.750
What're you looking for?!

00:19:53.750 --> 00:19:55.810
Are you trying to break my house?

00:19:56.750 --> 00:19:58.960
Oh, no, knock it off! Hey, that's my treasure!

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:00.550
Don't even touch it!

00:20:01.180 --> 00:20:02.220
Hey, are you listening?

00:20:04.790 --> 00:20:07.300
I've had enough of you people.

00:20:07.810 --> 00:20:09.770
Once was bad enough,

00:20:09.770 --> 00:20:11.760
but twice is unforgivable!

00:20:12.930 --> 00:20:14.740
What'd you say? Twice?

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:16.440
What do you mean?!

00:20:16.440 --> 00:20:18.400
You don't know?

00:20:18.700 --> 00:20:22.700
The military police were here looking 
for something a few days ago.

00:20:23.100 --> 00:20:26.450
Of course, they didn't find anything.

00:20:27.140 --> 00:20:28.910
What?

00:20:29.480 --> 00:20:32.830
<i>Then there's no chance we'll 
find any of the code ciphers.</i>

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:35.150
<i>The colonel knew, and he still...</i>

00:20:36.680 --> 00:20:38.910
<i>Even a tiny mistake is fine.</i>

00:20:38.910 --> 00:20:42.010
<i>If anything at all goes wrong, they're finished.</i>

00:20:42.580 --> 00:20:45.520
<i>But if nothing happens...</i>

00:20:47.370 --> 00:20:51.310
<i>The colonel did this on purpose 
to entrap D-Agency...</i>

00:20:52.490 --> 00:20:56.000
What's wrong? Going to keep searching?

00:20:57.820 --> 00:20:59.260
The kitchen is clear.

00:20:59.260 --> 00:21:00.600
The yard is clear.

00:21:00.900 --> 00:21:02.510
Drawers are clear.

00:21:02.910 --> 00:21:04.660
Above the ceiling is clear.

00:21:08.270 --> 00:21:10.290
<i>There wasn't anything here</i>

00:21:10.920 --> 00:21:13.120
<i>for us to find in the first place!</i>

00:21:14.570 --> 00:21:17.030
What's the matter, Captain-san?

00:21:17.030 --> 00:21:19.340
Is it show time now?

00:21:29.030 --> 00:21:30.120
<i>Don't tell me...</i>

00:21:38.550 --> 00:21:42.090
<i>I'm the one who ended up</i>

00:21:43.810 --> 00:21:46.580
<i>drawing the joker?!</i>

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:23.170
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:23.380 --> 00:23:24.790
What we're looking for

00:23:25.290 --> 00:23:27.840
may be closer than we think.

00:23:28.470 --> 00:23:29.550
What do you mean?

00:23:29.590 --> 00:23:34.880
Episode 2: Joker Game (Part 2)
